Z||000000||loafer87gt||02-29-2000||06:57 PM||||For the past week or so I have noticed that my car has really lost a lot of power, and will not rev above 4000 RPM. I took it into the GM dealership and they inspected the engine and said nother was wrong, except that my fuel injectors needed cleaning as they weren't flowing as much as they should be. Well, today leaving school my car refused to start, it turns over fine, but won't fire. The only thing iI noticed is a whining sound on the way there, could this be a fuel pump problem? Would this also cause the loss in power I'm experiencing? Thanks for any info... you guys are a grat help to mechanically inept guys like myself.||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||02-29-2000||07:40 PM||||sorry bout the double post. I must have hit the submit buttoin twice. oops||||reg||1
Z||000002||BENGAL4||02-29-2000||10:08 PM||||I think your catalytic converter is clogged. Mine did and it made a whirring sound also. I thought the rotor was hitting the distributor cap. It also had no power. replaced the cat, and everything was fine. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||02-29-2000||10:16 PM||||I cut the cat out when I did the exhaust on my car about 4 years ago. Thanks for the suggestion though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||03-01-2000||10:40 AM||||I figured out what the prob was. The distributor is shot. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||87SC/GT||03-01-2000||04:58 PM||||Here's my standard answer.. Low fuel pressure.Give it a shot of fuel in the manifold and see if it starts and runs.<BR>For some reason they will run with a weak <BR>pump if you can get it to start. Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000006||87SC/GT||03-01-2000||05:02 PM||||Or , err, ahh just replace the bad distributor. Sorry, didn't see the post about the distributor.||||reg||1
